items.body:
Closes #1182

Will make something like making a REST-adapter a lot easier as one could do `param: z.union([z.string(), z.number()]).transform(v => Number(v))` to handle query params.


**tl;dr** Allows us to do this below:

```tsx
trpc.router()
  .query('greeting', {
    input: z.object({
      hi: z.string().transform(s => s.length),
    }),
    resolve({ input }) {
      input.hi // => `number`, as expected
    },
  });

client.query('greeting', { hi: 'my greeting' }); 
```
